<p>Each metric keeps its own nondominated log-byte frontier, unchanged 0.25-unit bracket rule and no extrapolation. Frozen peers and all failed attempts remain in the evidence. Cached research files are excluded from public curves. Package ceilings and exports are preserved. This establishes no new speed or isolated RSS result. Fine checkpoint source SHA-256: <code>{fineProduction.implementationSourceSha256}</code>.</p>
<p>Fine allocation requires variation in the existing source importance scores. Inputs with nearly uniform source scores keep the preceding fine-quality path. All six published photo settings remain admitted. Their original files, decoder grids and quality scores are reused through an exact admission-only source bridge. The corrected complete packages are measured separately and remain within the original size ceilings. No photo was reencoded and no photo metric was refreshed for this guard correction.</p>
<p id="jxl-middle-channel-status">The qualified B-channel change reduces the portrait's matched Butteraugli-1 estimate by {middleReduction}%, to {Math.round(middleProduction.interpolatedBytes).toLocaleString('en-US')} bytes. It remains {middleGap('jsquash')}% larger than jSquash and {middleGap('vips')}% larger than wasm-vips. The Butteraugli-2 gap against jSquash at this checkpoint is 25.36%. The later Butteraugli-three result above keeps its own source and files. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/original-middle-channel-controls.json" download>Middle-photo public files and validation</a>.</p>
<p>Both complete public files match all natural-order coefficients and non-order geometry from the scored research files. Their learned scan orders differ legally. An original harness assertion required identical orders; its failed receipts remain preserved. Separate saved-file validation confirms exact native PNG identity before either quality score is reused. Full checks, the unchanged generated photo regression and real Chromium coverage pass. Fine and coarse paths retain their preceding behavior. No independent-photo middle curve or new speed and RSS result is claimed. Current source SHA-256: <code>{middleProduction.identity.implementationSourceSha256}</code>.</p>
<p id="jxl-cone-floor-status">The preceding middle/coarse curves reduce the portrait's matched Butteraugli-1 estimate by {conePortrait.reduction}%, to {coneSize(conePortrait.interpolatedBytes)} bytes. It remains {conePortraitGap('jsquash')}% larger than jSquash and {conePortraitGap('vips')}% larger than wasm-vips. The earlier original's Butteraugli-1 and SSIMULACRA2-90 comparisons also improve. The fine update above clears one of this checkpoint’s four confirmed gaps. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/original-cone-floor-controls.json" download>Preceding middle/coarse curves, source pins and preservation controls</a>.</p>
