<p>These scoped curves use {coneFloor.freshEncodedFiles} fresh complete public-package files, {coneFloor.freshCompleteIndependentGrids} complete native/Rust grids and {coneFloor.freshPublicDecodedSamples.toLocaleString('en-US')} checked public samples, with exact alpha and unchanged caller data. Additional tundra and Earthrise controls retain the exact baseline. Selection may encode a second candidate and keeps the smaller complete file, with baseline recovery on optional working-storage failure. This establishes neither a speed nor a memory improvement. Both metrics keep their own frontier, the original 0.25-unit bracket rule and no extrapolation. The peer encoders were not rerun; unresolved peer estimates remain unresolved. Preceding scoped source SHA-256: <code>{coneFloor.implementationSourceSha256}</code>.</p>
<p id="jxl-original-matrix-status">Overall lossy compression parity remains open. The historical unresized 2400 × 3000 portrait baseline uses {portraitMinimumGap}–{portraitMaximumGap}% more bytes than jSquash at three separately matched Butteraugli targets, despite competitive SSIMULACRA2 results. The earlier 12 MP photo results below keep their separate scope. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/ORIGINAL-MATRIX.md" download>Broader photo results and remaining gaps</a> and <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/original-matrix-portrait-baseline.json" download>Verified portrait baseline</a>.</p>
<p>The preceding median-luminance entropy change saves {entropyMinimumReduction}–{entropyMaximumReduction}% on six fixed-setting controls across the portrait, earlier photo, tundra and Earthrise originals, with identical decoded pixels and both quality scores. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/original-luma-context-controls.json" download>Median-luminance entropy controls</a>.</p>
<p id="jxl-spatial-context-status">The spatial histogram change saves another {spatialMinimumReduction}–{spatialMaximumReduction}% on five of those six controls. Earthrise keeps the preceding bytes. Every decoded pixel and both quality scores remain identical. This adds encoding work and does not close the portrait's matched-quality gaps. The historical tables below retain their earlier curve source; the latest scoped curves are shown separately. Spatial source SHA-256: <code>{spatialControls.implementationSourceSha256}</code>. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/original-spatial-context-controls.json" download>Spatial entropy preservation controls</a>.</p>
<p>On the original 4000 × 3000 photo, PureJsImage uses 9–13% fewer bytes than jSquash and 8–16% fewer than wasm-vips at matched SSIMULACRA2 70, 80 and 90. It also uses fewer bytes at all four matched Butteraugli targets against jSquash and both resolved targets against wasm-vips; two wasm-vips targets remain unresolved under the unchanged rules. Parity applies to the resolved targets on this photo; other original-size photos, HDR, float, CMYK and animation need separate matched compression evidence. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/ORIGINAL-PHOTO.md" download>Original-size photo results and limits</a> and <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/original-photo-production-controls.json" download>Original checkpoint production controls</a>.</p>
